(# Optimization matrix: spam / fp32) Tj
T*
(Status: COMPLETE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Design: 27 off/best/poor combinations plus four jointly selected attention/cache cases.) Tj
T*
(Best and poor are observed finite-grid choices. Training configurations were fixed from prior validation.) Tj
T*
(Poor LoRA was selected by worst seed-42 full-budget validation loss, then retrained on three seeds.) Tj
T*
(Off LoRA means the selected full-fine-tuning control; this is not an unadapted pretrained model.) Tj
T*
(Attention/cache best and poor are calibrated independently per checkpoint and workload; joint cases use) Tj
T*
(paired settings.) Tj
T*
(Calibration uses a distinct prompt stream and three timings; confirmation uses seven timings and three) Tj
T*
(training seeds.) Tj
T*
(Strict parity is checked against each checkpoint on eager/no-cache, not between different trained) Tj
T*
(checkpoints.) Tj
T*
(Failures remain diagnostic. Complete artifact coverage does not mean every optimization passed) Tj
T*
(correctness.) Tj
T*
(Task quality uses natural held-out examples with canonical serving choices \(batch 1, prompt 128, output) Tj
T*
(32\).) Tj
T*
(SMS is a one-step label task; its cache benefit is assessed only by synthetic serving workloads.) Tj
T*
(Timing SD within an allocation and variation across model seeds are not independent hardware) Tj
T*
(replications.) Tj
T*
(Original data splits are reused; full/LoRA inherited tuning search budgets are unequal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
